From d40192cfcc27f0bec2b689fa3a26f5b9901460d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:13:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 51/88] h713: hdmi: an acknowledged restart keeps the HDMI
 bytes of the page

A firmware restart while awake zeroed the whole page outside the diag
words, the HPD counters, ready, gate and mask bytes and the port map
included, and cleared the EDID-module bit - while the aux clock, the
pin, the gate and the DDC RAM kept their state. Afterwards hpd_pin() saw
gate 0 and held the pin low, a pulse under way never ended, and a
HostHDMIMAP was lost (PRUEFUNG5 F2).

When the restart is acknowledged (Linux took the notify), +0x010..+0x0ff
stays (contract v5, class R), portmap_init() is skipped, and the status
bit comes from the hardware (aux_clocked()). edid[] is gone with .bss,
so publish() waits for the next upload; until then the DDC RAM keeps
what it served. The kernel's side - noticing the restart and replaying
the EDID - is A5 of the release design.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c b/drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c
index 2a39614..617dfdd 100644
--- a/drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c
@@ -873,10 +873,19 @@ h713_init(void)
 	 * Contract v5 (platform/memory.h): R and S at every start; K and X
 	 * only at the first one after a load (a v4 kernel zeroes the diag
 	 * words, not K), so the record survives an exception restart. D, A
-	 * and P are the loaders'.
+	 * and P are the loaders'. An acknowledged restart also keeps R's
+	 * HDMI bytes (+0x010..+0x0ff: HPD counters, ready, gate, mask, port
+	 * map): the aux block, the pin and the DDC RAM keep their state
+	 * across it, so a pulse under way ends and the pin can rise again
+	 * (PRUEFUNG5 F2). edid[] is gone with .bss; publish() waits for the
+	 * next upload.
 	 */
 	for (uintptr_t a = H713_SHARED_BASE; a < H713_SEEN_LIMIT; a += 4) {
-		if (a < H713_DIAG_BASE || a >= H713_DIAG_LIMIT)
+		bool kept = (a >= H713_DIAG_BASE && a < H713_DIAG_LIMIT) ||
+		            (acked && a >= H713_R_KEPT_BASE &&
+		             a < H713_R_KEPT_LIMIT);
+
+		if (!kept)
 			mmio_write_32(a, 0);
 	}
 	for (uintptr_t a = H713_K_BASE; first && a < H713_SHARED_LIMIT; a += 4) {
@@ -912,7 +921,10 @@ h713_init(void)
 	mmio_write_32(H713_K_BUILD2, (BUILD2_DRAM_MHZ & 0xfff) |
 	              (CONFIG_H713_BOARD_ID & 0xf) << 12 |
 	              (BUILD2_NET_CODE & 0xff) << 16);
-	portmap_init();
+	if (!acked)
+		portmap_init();
+	if (aux_clocked())	/* hardware state, also after a restart */
+		sh_status(ST_EDID_MODULE, 0);
 	/*
 	 * Load-bearing: system.c puts its own msgbox reference at every
 	 * suspend, and a last put would assert the msgbox reset (ccu.c); this
